# Unified-Field Solver — Experimental Analysis Phase
### Author: C. Matthew Blackwell

The Unified-Field Solver is an experimental cosmology analysis engine designed to
extract hidden, non-Gaussian residual structure from real sky data (Planck CMB,
SDSS galaxy fields) using a harmonic-relaxation baseline model.

The solver implements the equation:

    ∇²T_sim = 1 / (2λ)

and computes the residual field:

    ΔT = |T_obs - T_sim|

This residual isolates structure normally suppressed by ΛCDM smoothing pipelines.
The system includes:

- Harmonic-relaxation PDE solver
- Residual isolation engine
- Power-spectrum analysis (P(k))
- Dark-sector interpretation modules
- Noether-style energy conservation audit
- Cryptographic integrity layer (XOR + quantum-resistant hashing)

